"The Rapport School on Rapport I teaches knights' children of all ages until university."
"It sits near Root, the Rapport's one town, and offers adult classes on request."
"It is built partway up a slope: three floors, a flat railed roof and two squat domed towers."
"Its summonarium has separate teleport circles for people and objects, labeled in dark pink paint."
"A boarders' tower houses students, and a wall of packed dirt is latticed with tree roots."
"A self-lighting staircase climbs the hillside; the front lawn has a bare circle for games."
"Its library tower has a glass-walled winding stair up to the 'top library'."
"The top library shelves stone recorder cubes, spheres and pyramids; quiet is not expected there."
"Root-woven ladders reach a balcony of instructors' cabinets holding student study journals."
"A wall of angle-dependent paintings shows knights fighting chaos."
"A supply room stocks wands, rings, paper and brushes, and first meal of fruit and wevvi."
"A room of magical teaching tools supplies practice rings."
"Rel-art'h teaches there and directs newling squads on missions."
"Its summonarium has an arrivals board, a building map and student benches along the windows."
"It has a lantern-lit courtyard, a student house and a long staircase of glowing steps."
"Stuart grew a patch of grass on the grounds for bokabv games."
